course: dictionary
lesson: 1103
title: Bran: the outer layer of grain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word bran is a good example. It can be a thing you eat, or it can be a name. «White rice is brown rice with the outer layers, called bran, polished off.» Here the words "outer layers" and "polished off" are the clues. They show that bran is a part of the grain that gets removed.
explain: Look at the words around the word. In a sentence about breakfast or healthy food, bran means the food part. In a sentence about a person or a legend, Bran is a name, and it starts with a capital letter. A capital letter in the middle of a sentence is a clue that you are reading a name.
explain: Ask what the word does in the sentence. In «The bran held vitamin B1», bran is something that holds something else, so it must be a real thing in the grain. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. If "the outer layer of grain held vitamin B1" still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Bran is the brown outer layer of grains such as wheat and oats.
fact: Bran comes off when flour is made.
fact: Bran is full of fibre, which helps your digestion.
fact: Brown rice keeps its bran, and white rice has had its bran polished off.
fact: Bran is also a name in Welsh and Irish legends, so it has a capital letter.
exercise: «White rice is brown rice with the outer layers, called bran, polished off.» What is bran in this sentence? | A kind of sugar | The white centre of a grain | *The outer layer of a grain | A type of rice that cooks slowly
exercise: Bran is full of which good thing for your digestion? | Oil | Sugar | *Fibre | Salt
exercise: «Bran is a name in Welsh and Irish legends.» In this sentence, what kind of word is Bran? | A verb | A food | *A name | A colour
test: Why does white rice cook faster than brown rice? | It has more bran than brown rice | *Its bran has been polished off | It has been dyed white | Bran makes rice cook slower and it is missing
test: At an old fair, a «bran tub» held hidden prizes. What was in the tub? | *Bran with hidden prizes | Water with hidden prizes | Sweets only | Sand with hidden prizes
exam: Which word means the outer layer of grain that comes off when flour is made? | Flour | *Bran | Yeast | Sugar
